===Switzerland===
Manager: [[Köbi Kuhn]]

Switzerland named an initial 26-man squad on 24 May 2004.<ref>{{cite news |title=Swiss recall striker Thurre |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/euro_2004/switzerland/3743387.stm |website=BBC Sport|publisher=BBC|date=24 May 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref> [[Stéphane Grichting]] and [[Rémo Meyer]] were both cut from the final squad, while [[Marco Streller]] broke his left tibia and fibula and [[Léonard Thurre]] tore a calf muscle in training;<ref>{{cite news |title=Swiss striker Streller misses out |url=http://www.espnfc.com/print?id=301955&type=story|website=ESPN FC|publisher=ESPN|date=30 May 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Swiss Streller out for six months |url=http://www.espnfc.com/news/story?id=302187&cc=5739|website=ESPN FC |publisher=ESPN|date=2 June 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref> they were replaced in the final 23-man squad by 18-year-old [[PSV Eindhoven]] forward [[Johan Vonlanthen]].<ref>{{cite news |title=PSV ace gets Swiss call-up |url=http://www1.skysports.com/football/news/11914/2300913/psv-ace-gets-swiss-call-up|website=[[Sky Sports]]|publisher=Sky Group|date=1 June 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref>

On 6 June, midfielder [[Johann Lonfat]] was withdrawn from the squad after suffering a back injury; he was originally going to be replaced by [[Juventus FC|Juventus]] forward [[Davide Chiumiento]], but he declined the selection in favour of waiting for a call-up by [[Italy national football team|Italy]], meaning that [[Tranquillo Barnetta]] replaced Lonfat instead.<ref>{{cite news |first=Marco |last=Keller |title=Barnetta steps up for Swiss |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7b43e33779-15fe4badbd3c-1000--barnetta-steps-up-for-swiss/|website=UEFA|date=6 June 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref> Goalkeeper [[Fabrice Borer]] suffered a broken arm in training on 12 June and was replaced by [[Sébastien Roth]] before Switzerland's opening game against [[Croatia national football team|Croatia]] the next day.<ref>{{cite news |title=Swiss keeper breaks arm |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/euro_2004/switzerland/3803027.stm |website=BBC Sport|publisher=BBC|date=13 June 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref>

