===Germany===
Manager: [[Rudi Völler]]

Germany named an initial 22-man squad on 24 May 2004, with coach [[Rudi Völler]] leaving one space open for an under-21 player.<ref>{{cite news |first=James |last=Pearson |title=Voller unveils 22-man Germany squad |url=http://www1.skysports.com/FIFA-World-Cup-2014/news/12023/2299978/voller-unveils-22-man-germany-squad|website=Sky Sport|publisher=BBC|date=24 May 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref> [[Hamburger SV]] defender [[Christian Rahn]] withdrew from the squad on 26 May and was replaced by left-back [[Christian Ziege]], who had recently been released by [[Tottenham Hotspur F.C.|Tottenham Hotspur]].<ref>{{cite news |title=Rahn withdrawal benefits Ziege |url=https://www.uefa.com/uefaeuro/history/news/0254-0d7b28018698-1fb0c300083c-1000--rahn-withdrawal-benefits-ziege/|website=UEFA|date=26 May 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref> [[VfL Bochum]] winger [[Paul Freier]] was also ruled out on 29 May after damaging knee ligaments in a warm-up friendly against [[Malta national football team|Malta]] on 27 May;<ref>{{cite news |title=Freier out of Euro 2004 |url=http://news.bbc.co.uk/sport1/hi/football/internationals/3760451.stm |website=BBC Sport|publisher=BBC|date=29 May 2004 |access-date=23 May 2014 }}</ref> his withdrawal allowed both early contenders for the 23rd place in the squad, [[Bastian Schweinsteiger]] and [[Lukas Podolski]], to be selected.

